Package: swaydesk-session-menu
Architecture: any
Depends: swaydesk-common (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: swaydesk-lock
Breaks: swaydesk-desktop (<< 0.1.7~), swaydesk-session (<< 0.1.7~)
Replaces: swaydesk-desktop (<< 0.1.7~), swaydesk-session (<< 0.1.7~)
Description: Swaydesk session menu (lock, log out, suspend, restart, shut down)
 Lock, log out, suspend, restart and shut down, full screen. When an app
 asks to restart or shut down, it asks first, with a countdown.

# python3, GTK 3 and gtk-session-lock: the Python lock (sway-lock-gtk) is the real lock on Debian 13, whose
# gtk4-layer-shell has no session lock before 1.2 (install-tree.sh ships it on Debian and Ubuntu only)
Package: swaydesk-lock
Architecture: any
Depends: swaydesk-common (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd, libpam0g, gtklock, python3, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gtksessionlock-0.1
Recommends: swayidle, libnotify-bin
Breaks: swaydesk-desktop (<< 0.1.7~), swaydesk-scripts (<< 0.1.7~), swaydesk-session (<< 0.1.7~)
Replaces: swaydesk-desktop (<< 0.1.7~), swaydesk-scripts (<< 0.1.7~), swaydesk-session (<< 0.1.7~)
Description: Swaydesk lock screen
 Time, date and the password field on every monitor, over the blurred
 wallpaper. It checks the password with its own PAM service
 (/etc/pam.d/swaydesk-lock). Where gtk4-layer-shell is older than 1.2
 (Debian 13), the lock is sway-lock-gtk, the same lock in Python with
 GTK 3. gtklock is the fallback locker.

Package: swaydesk-keyring
Architecture: any
Depends: swaydesk-common (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd
Breaks: swaydesk-desktop (<< 0.1.7~), swaydesk-session (<< 0.1.7~)
Replaces: swaydesk-desktop (<< 0.1.7~), swaydesk-session (<< 0.1.7~)
Description: Swaydesk keyring fix
 Fixes the keyring of a user's first login when gnome-keyring creates it
 but doesn't publish it on D-Bus (Debian 13): it asks for the password once,
 and from then on the keyring opens with the login. Otherwise it does
 nothing.

Package: swaydesk-sessionmgr
Architecture: any
Depends: swaydesk-common (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, sway
Recommends: swaydesk-session-menu
Breaks: swaydesk-desktop (<< 0.1.7~), swaydesk-session (<< 0.1.7~)
Replaces: swaydesk-desktop (<< 0.1.7~), swaydesk-session (<< 0.1.7~)
Description: Swaydesk session manager service
 A minimal org.gnome.SessionManager for Sway, so GNOME Software can
 restart or shut down after updates. With swaydesk-session-menu, it asks
 first, with a countdown. Without swaydesk-session-menu, it restarts or
 shuts down when asked, with no confirmation.

